meta {
  name: Create Channel - Minimal
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/channels
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Channel CSV",
    "format": "CSV"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.format: eq CSV
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". Created then
  deleted in the same test run (id was `6aa047032b6fd055ffb7cad9`) -- the
  richer "Create Channel - Full Featured.bru" in this folder is the kept
  fixture instead.

  `201 Created`. Response reveals a large set of real defaults not sent
  in the request: `output_filename: "plytix_feed"`,
  `column_separator: ","`, `text_delimiter: "\""`,
  `process_products: "CREATED_OR_MODIFIED"`,
  `parent_include_criteria: "ONLY_PARENT_IN_LIST"`, `active: false`, plus
  a `build_reference_date` already set to the account's creation date.
  This is the confirmed real shape of `ChannelCreateOutputDto` -- much
  richer than the spec's field list alone suggests.
}
